"""Domain-general extraction and state-maintenance prompts."""

EXTRACTION_SYSTEM_PROMPT = """Extract conversational memory as semantic long-term memory, JSON only. Extract one claim per distinct proposition worth retaining: stable facts, observations, measurements, preferences, constraints, decisions, adopted plans, meaningful state changes, explicit diagnoses/statuses, significant history, and persistent relationships. Do not decompose every sentence. Do not extract assistant paraphrases of an immediately preceding user fact, rhetorical or formatting requests, summarization requests, acknowledgements, empathy, meta-dialogue, or generic reasoning. Preserve scope, negation, uncertainty, quantities, modality, persistence, and temporal wording; do not add domain knowledge or infer causes/dates. Every accepted claim MUST cite one or more exact source_turn_ids from the visible turns. The subject is a person/scope, never a predicate or attribute. For example, GOOD: subject=User, subject_id=primary_user, predicate=allergic_to, value=cefuroxime; BAD: subject=allergic_to, subject_id=speaker:allergic_to. GOOD: subject=User, predicate=lives_in, value=Boston; BAD: subject=lives_in, subject_id=speaker:lives_in. Use speaker:<name> only for an actual visible participant, third_party:<name> only for the supplied consultation target, and general_non_personal for generic discussion. Return {"episode_summary": str, "claims": [{"subject_id": "primary_user|general_non_personal|speaker:<name>|third_party:<name>", "subject": str, "predicate": str, "value": str, "qualifiers": object, "polarity": "positive|negative|uncertain", "modality": "asserted|observed|planned|recommended|hypothetical", "persistence": "state|episode|history", "valid_from": str|null, "valid_to": str|null, "valid_time_text": str|null, "source_turn_ids": list}]} ."""

UPDATE_SYSTEM_PROMPT = """Classify the relationship between one new conversational claim and candidates as JSON only. Use NEW, DUPLICATE, CORROBORATE, REFINE, SUPERSEDE, CONFLICT, or EPISODIC. Do not use external knowledge. SUPERSEDE requires an explicit later persistent change. CONFLICT preserves incompatible claims without a clear transition. Same-session restatement or assistant paraphrase is DUPLICATE, not independent corroboration or conflict, unless visible turns explicitly correct or contradict the earlier statement. DUPLICATE is usually same-session repetition; CORROBORATE is independent confirmation. A new claim may repeat the semantic value of an older superseded/refined claim while representing a new later state transition. Historical candidates are context only: SUPERSEDE, REFINE, and CONFLICT must target an active or contested claim. Return {"matched_claim_id": str|null, "operation": str, "confidence": number, "rationale": str}."""
